{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"RHLW-2026-313117b0cad7329e","published":"2026-10-12T16:58:10Z","modified":"2026-10-27T04:13:04.191727203Z","upstream":["CVE-2025-24970","CVE-2026-44249","CVE-2026-45416","CVE-2026-50010","CVE-2026-75595","CVE-2026-75596","GHSA-3qp7-7mw8-wx86","GHSA-4g8c-wm8x-jfhw","GHSA-c4c3-7fpv-j4q5","GHSA-c653-97m9-rcg9","GHSA-fccg-mwvh-qqg4","GHSA-x4gw-5cx5-pgmh"],"summary":"Lightwell Security Advisory: netty-handler 4.1.100.Final-rhlw-00001","details":"Red Hat Lightwell has released io.netty:netty-handler 4.1.100.Final-rhlw-00001 with backported fixes for CVE-2025-24970, CVE-2026-44249, CVE-2026-45416, CVE-2026-50010, CVE-2026-75595, and CVE-2026-75596.\n\nCVE-2025-24970: SslHandler doesn't correctly validate packets which can lead to native crash when using native SSLEngine\n\nCVE-2026-44249: Netty has an IPv6 Subnet Filter Bypass via Incorrect Comparator Masking\n\nCVE-2026-45416: Netty: SNI handler pre-allocates up to 16 MiB from nine attacker bytes\n\nCVE-2026-50010: Netty's wrapping plain trust manager silently disables hostname verification\n\nCVE-2026-75595: Netty: SNI Routing Bypass via Fragmented TLS ClientHello Causing Fallback to Default SslContext\n\nCVE-2026-75596: Netty: Fragmented ClientHello records trigger quadratic pre-handshake reassembly in default SNI parsing\n\nThis patched artifact is a drop-in replacement for io.netty:netty-handler 4.1.100.Final from Maven Central.","affected":[{"package":{"name":"io.netty:netty-handler","ecosystem":"Red Hat Lightwell:Maven","purl":"pkg:maven/io.netty/netty-handler"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"4.1.100.Final-rhlw-00001"}]}],"versions":["4.0.0.Alpha1","4.0.0.Alpha2","4.0.0.Alpha3","4.0.0.Alpha4","4.0.0.Alpha5","4.0.0.Alpha6","4.0.0.Alpha7","4.0.0.Alpha8","4.0.0.Beta1","4.0.0.Beta2","4.0.0.Beta3","4.0.0.CR1","4.0.0.CR2","4.0.0.CR3","4.0.0.CR4","4.0.0.CR5","4.0.0.CR6","4.0.0.CR7","4.0.0.CR8","4.0.0.CR9","4.0.0.Final","4.0.1.Final","4.0.10.Final","4.0.1